Track 2: Sump-Level Confession
- Story & Context: In the deepest, wettest sump-level chamber, where the air was thick with minerals, older miner Rhys confessed his fear of never seeing his daughter's face again to the reverberating silence, the metallic clang of a loose pipe resonating his despair, but also an odd, grounding comfort. "My map was wrong, darling, but the stars still burn."
